From 143bebeac615f9d2fcc44b711d677cfb52c8e4c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Dutton <chris@bigcove.io>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 11:41:46 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 16/18] firmware: demote SoftAP admission diagnostics to debug
 level; README: state the esp-hosted library dependency precisely

The firmware never linked against stock ESP-IDF (ieee80211_add_node and
esp_wifi_send_assoc_internal only exist in esp-hosted NG's build of the
Wi-Fi libraries), so describe it as the build requirement it is rather than
as a behavioural difference.
---
 README.md                         | 18 +++++++++---------
 firmware/main/trellis_wifi_ap.c   |  2 +-
 firmware/main/trellis_wifi_host.c | 10 +++++-----
 3 files changed, 15 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 2056442..4e3534e 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -44,12 +44,12 @@ everything above the driver - no bespoke radio API to integrate against.
 ### Firmware toolchain: ESP-IDF v5.5.1 with esp-hosted NG's Wi-Fi libraries
 
 The host-SME WiFi model (hostapd/wpa_supplicant on Linux run the AP
-authenticator and the STA SME) depends on hooks that only exist in the
-Wi-Fi libraries Espressif ships with **esp-hosted NG**, not in stock ESP-IDF:
-the `WIFI_APPIE_RAM_BEACON_PROBE_HEAD/TAIL` beacon slots and
-`ieee80211_send_mgmt_internal()` among them. A firmware built on stock IDF
-links fine but the SoftAP never beacons and clients can never associate
-(verified on hardware, 2026-10-09). Set the toolchain up exactly as
+authenticator and the STA SME) uses entry points that only exist in the
+build of Espressif's closed Wi-Fi libraries shipped with **esp-hosted NG**:
+`ieee80211_add_node()`, `ieee80211_send_mgmt_internal()`,
+`esp_wifi_send_assoc_internal()`, the beacon head/tail IE slots and others
+(17 symbols absent from stock ESP-IDF 5.5.1's `libnet80211.a`). The firmware
+does not link against stock IDF at all. Set the toolchain up exactly as
 esp-hosted does, on the same IDF commit:
 
 ```sh
@@ -64,9 +64,9 @@ rm -rf components/esp_wifi/lib/* && cp -r <esp-hosted>/esp_hosted_ng/esp/esp_dri
 
 (`<esp-hosted>` is a checkout of https://github.com/espressif/esp-hosted at
 `release/ng-1.0.6`; its `esp_hosted_ng/esp/esp_driver/.env` pins the IDF
-commit above.) A correctly built image contains the patched library's
-version string `d34ae1d`; stock IDF 5.5.1 reports `bad379d` on the ESP32's
-console at boot (`wifi firmware version:`).
+commit above.) The ESP32 prints the library revision at boot
+(`wifi firmware version:`); 1.0.6's `libnet80211` is `d34ae1d`, stock IDF
+5.5.1's is `14da9b7`.
 
 Build with the preset wrapper (`idf.py --preset` is an IDF 6 feature):
 
diff --git a/firmware/main/trellis_wifi_ap.c b/firmware/main/trellis_wifi_ap.c
index 994d00e..417529a 100644
--- a/firmware/main/trellis_wifi_ap.c
+++ b/firmware/main/trellis_wifi_ap.c
@@ -419,7 +419,7 @@ void trellis_wifi_ap_data_rx(uint16_t flags, const uint8_t *chunk, uint16_t chun
 
     err = esp_wifi_internal_tx(WIFI_IF_AP, s_ap_data_reasm.buf, frame_len);
     if (frame_len >= 14 && s_ap_data_reasm.buf[12] == 0x88 && s_ap_data_reasm.buf[13] == 0x8e)
-        ESP_LOGI(TAG, "ap tx EAPOL %u bytes -> %d", frame_len, err);
+        ESP_LOGD(TAG, "ap tx EAPOL %u bytes -> %d", frame_len, err);
     if (err != 0)
         ESP_LOGW(TAG, "esp_wifi_internal_tx failed: %d (%u bytes)", err, frame_len);
 
